┌───────────────────────────┐  
│ Quick Definition          │  
│                           │  
│ Uniform acceleration is a │  
│ type of motion where the  │  
│ acceleration of an object  │  
│ remains constant over time.│  
└───────────────────────────┘  

┌───────────────────────────┐  
│ Key Concepts              │  
│                           │  
│ - In uniform acceleration, │  
│   the velocity of an      │  
│   object increases or      │  
│   decreases at a steady    │  
│   rate.                   │  
│ - The motion can be       │  
│   described using the      │  
│   equations of motion.     │  
└───────────────────────────┘  

┌───────────────────────────┐  
│ Main Formula              │  
│                           │  
│ The formula for           │  
│ uniform acceleration is:  │  
│                           │  
│ $$s = ut + \frac{1}{2} a t^2$$ │  
│                           │  
│ Where:                   │  
│ - \(s\) is the distance   │  
│   traveled.               │  
│ - \(u\) is the initial    │  
│   velocity.               │  
│ - \(a\) is the constant   │  
│   acceleration.           │  
│ - \(t\) is the time.     │  
│                           │  
│ [ Explain Formula ]       │  
│ [ Open Formula Lab ]      │  
└───────────────────────────┘  

┌───────────────────────────┐  
│ Applications              │  
│                           │  
│ Uniform acceleration is   │  
│ commonly observed in      │  
│ various scenarios such as  │  
│ free fall, vehicles on    │  
│ a straight road, and      │  
│ certain types of motion    │  
│ in physics experiments.    │  
└───────────────────────────┘  

┌───────────────────────────┐  
│ Important Notes           │  
│                           │  
│ - The concept assumes no  │  
│   external forces acting   │  
│   on the object except for │  
│   gravity in free fall.   │  
│ - Uniform acceleration is  │  
│   different from uniform   │  
│   motion, where speed is   │  
│   constant.               │  
└───────────────────────────┘  

┌───────────────────────────┐  
│ Summary                  │  
│                           │  
│ Uniform acceleration is a │  
│ fundamental concept in    │  
│ physics that describes     │  
│ motion with a constant     │  
│ rate of change in velocity.│  
│ The associated formula     │  
│ helps in calculating       │  
│ distances and understanding │  
│ the behavior of moving     │  
│ objects.                  │  
└───────────────────────────┘  

┌───────────────────────────┐  
│ Suggested Questions       │  
│                           │  
